sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 25-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite (referee re-score) faithfully reproduces None. No organism, tissue, cell population, specimen image or experimental dataset is loaded or compared; the claimed subjects (bioelectric collectives, GRNs, active matter) appear only in comments and law titles morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean, morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real None. No organism, tissue, cell population, specimen image or experimental dataset is loaded or compared; the claimed subjects (bioelectric collectives, GRNs, active matter) appear only in comments and law titles specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 26.4/100, audit 2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json; output: media/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png; organism: None. No organism, tissue, cell population, specimen image or experimental dataset is loaded or compared; the claimed subjects (bioelectric collectives, GRNs, active matter) appear only in comments and law titles; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/bfe377c2; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, lean 4.35.0; spec_fingerprint: cf19761e9e6760d1e706dce6a8fdea337079e70d318494d21ee724915d6bb697; artifact_sha256: 2e2cd28df81d42a235a6c03f640c7a351859e4a4f758ee4692323ad541edbfaa; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json=38aab3be23160a82..., datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib=5acabab1711c1899...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Levin (2019, 2022): TAME cognitive-light-cone framework (diagrammatic, no closed-form R_eff(N, G_gj) is published) | Chvykov et al. (2021) Science 371:90: low-rattling stationary measure P_ss(x) ~ r(x)^(-gamma) tested on robotic 'smarticle' collectives | Bongard & Levin (2023) Biomimetics 8:110: polycomputing as a conceptual framework (no XOR/AND/OR state-map equation is published) | Pigozzi, Goldstein & Levin (2025) Commun. Biol. 8:1027: associative conditioning in continuous GRN ODE models; Watson & Szathmary (2016) TREE 31:147: natural induction / Hebbian attractor deepening | Rosas et al. (2019) Phys. Rev. E 100:032305: O-information Omega(X^n); Scheibner et al. (2020) / Tan et al. (2022): odd elasticity and chiral crystal work cycles; Gilbert & Mosteller (1966): the 1/e secretary-problem law | Pietak & Levin (2016, 2017): Nernst-Planck electrodiffusion in BETSE; Cervera, Levin & Mafe: voltage-gated gap-junction bistability (cited in the KG without DOI); reconstructed_in_script: 25 scalar quantities evaluated once each at hard-coded constants (L49-L200); a 24-state power-law table and its own log-log fit (Law 5, L72-L77); a 99-term secretary-problem sum (Law 7, L84-L89); a 4-row x 3-gate truth table (Law 8, L91-L96) | A `laws_summary` list (L202-L228) assigning each law an `equation_origin` (O1/O2), an `epistemic_tier` (T1-T4), a `criteria_passed` list (C1-C5), video IDs, the computed `metric` and a `ref` that is, for 23 of 25 laws, the same expression or its rounded value | An 8-panel figure (L244-L377) whose panels 5, 6 and 8 plot analytic decoration curves (10 exp(-0.8 t), a piecewise sine for ln|S|, exp(-0.4 t), 0.5^(t/2), exp(-0.6 t) cos(1.2 t)) that are not produced by any computation in verify_all_25_laws() | 25 Lean 4 theorems in Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean (0 sorry; 2 exhaustive Bool proofs, 10 trivially-universal identities paired with ground constants, 13 ground `decide` checks); 6 earlier theorems in MathOfBiology.lean section 16; transfer_boundary: Every dynamical law in the titles (Cervera gap-junction ODE, Nernst-Planck PDE, Chvykov Markov jump process, Brenner Langevin SDE, Friston gradient flow, Weinberg Ca2+ integral-feedback ODE, Rebbin cable equation, Guichard NCA) is replaced by a single algebraic consequence evaluated at one point; none is integrated, so no regime, bifurcation, threshold or breakdown horizon (criterion C4) is actually exhibited | The S_6 causal-emergence numbers in Law 17 (0.8687, 0.0191, 1.0000, 0.0313, 0.7209, 0.1238) are copied from the repository's own earlier sorting-morphogenesis run (sorting-morphogenesis/PLATONIC_SPACE_CLAIMS_EVALUATION.md L112-L118), not recomputed and not from Hoel (2026) | Law 5's slope of -1.0000 is guaranteed by construction (p_ss is defined as r_exit^-1 / Z at L75); it tests numpy.polyfit, not Chvykov's law | Law 7's Python optimum (k* = 37, P = 0.37104) is the classical secretary problem; its Lean theorem brackets 100566 = 37 x 2718 rather than 100 x 1000 (floor(100000/2718) = 36), so the machine-checked statement is not floor(N/e) = 37 | Law 16's Python metric (Shannon-Hartley capacity 2.0 bits at SNR 15, L136-L139) and its Lean theorem (E_total - E_maint - E_info = 30, Loop L251-L258) are different equations; the measurement sidecar reports the former under the latter's theorem name | The video catalog is metadata only (titles, durations, views, descriptions, a stale 6-law `mappedMathLaws` field); no transcript, slide or figure text is parsed, so 'extracted from the channel' is a manual attribution, not a reproducible extraction; does_not_claim: This referee audit does not claim any of the 25 source equations is wrong as published; it scores whether the suite implements, exercises and validates them, and whether the O1/O2, T1-T4 and C1-C5 tags are earned by the artefacts | It does not verify the content of the 72 referenced videos (no transcripts are available offline) and does not re-derive the S_6 causal-emergence numbers | It does not claim the Lean modules fail: both compile with 0 sorry; the finding is about what the theorems state, not whether they check]; other sources: KAN: Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks <https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.19756>, Mortal Computation: A Foundation for Biomimetic Intelligence <https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.09589>, A Neural Cellular Automaton Model of Memory Transfer <https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.11855>, Extended Iterated, Spatialized Prisoner's Dilemma: Game Theory of Multicellularity with Agent-Controlled Borders <https://osf.io/kpzju_v2>, datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json - 374-video metadata index of @drmichaellevin <https://www.youtube.com/@drmichaellevin>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
